 {
  "coord": "13:47",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "grammar",
  "note": "\"For that the heavens...\" reads as a fragment; the sin is the antecedent.",
  "replacement": "LEONTES. May the blessed gods purge all infection from our air while you live in this climate! You have a holy father, a gracious gentleman, against whose person, sacred as it is, I have sinned. For that sin the heavens, taking angry note, have left me without children. And your father is blessed, as he deserves from heaven, with you, who are worthy of his goodness. What might I have been, if I could now have looked on a son and daughter, such goodly things as you!"
 },
